<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Moquihuix</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1473</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Moquihuix was the tlatoani of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tlatelolco">Tlatelolco</a>, the twin city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a>, from about 1460 to 1473. He was married to a sister of the Tenochca ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axayacatl">Axayacatl</a>, and quarrels between the two cities led to open war in 1473. Axayacatl's forces stormed Tlatelolco and Moquihuix died, by tradition thrown from the top of its main temple, after which the city lost its own rulers and was placed under a military governor.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/moquihuix.jpg" alt="Moquihuix" width="320" height="336" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Moquihuix_mendoza.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
